  Sigh.

  I finally ascended (first time, no cheating other than a few "curious"
questions here)!  It was pure luck, nothing else; the correct altar and
a magic lamp in the gnomish mines, two magic lamps in a shop back in the
regular dungeon, a friendly throne, and a large scroll shop with 3 SoGs
(one blessed) make a big difference. I even had a couple wishes left in
my wand when I finished :-)

  So it listed my equipment, intrinsics, monsters killed, genocides, and
finally score.

  Then the screen cleared, and it said,

Waiting for access to record.  (59 retries left)

  In horror, I watched it count down to zero, and give up.  Poof.  So
much for a chance to show off... :-\

  This sort of thing occasionally happens with nethack, and there isn't
much one can do around here other than asking one of the games admins to
fix it.

  So would it be possible to add something to nethack, such that if it
can't record the score it saves a "saved game" that, when restarted,
attempts to save the score again?

  Oh well.

